<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sha'irum Awtar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Shaʿir Awtar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sha'irum Awtar was a king of Saba and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-raydan">Dhu Raydan</a> in the early third century CE, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a>. His inscriptions record victories over Hadramawt, including the capture and burning of its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shabwa">Shabwa</a>, and campaigns against Himyar and the Aksumite forces then active in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. He was among the last Sabaean kings to win major wars before Himyar absorbed Saba.</p></div>
